<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Deliberately ONE url, and it needs explaining rather than expanding.

  This site is hash-routed: every page is #/product, #/composition and so on.
  A fragment is never sent to a server, so those are not separate URLs and a
  crawler cannot be given them here. Listing them would be listing URLs that do
  not exist. If the site ever moves to real paths (see the trade-off note in
  src/router.jsx), this file grows to one <url> per route and not before.

  Note also that public/robots.txt currently disallows everything, because PULP
  cannot be advertised to the public before NPRA product notification and KKLIU
  approval. While that is true this sitemap is intentionally inert, and it is not
  referenced from robots.txt — announcing a sitemap while disallowing the whole
  site is a contradiction that makes both look like mistakes.

  AT LAUNCH: remove the Disallow from robots.txt, remove the noindex meta from
  index.html, add `Sitemap: https://pulp.my/sitemap.xml` to robots.txt, and add a
  <lastmod> below.

  No <lastmod> element here on purpose: it is optional, and the placeholder text
  this file would otherwise carry is not a valid xsd:date, which would make the
  whole sitemap fail validation. An absent optional element beats an invalid one.
-->
<urlset xmlns="http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9">
  <url>
    <loc>https://pulp.my/</loc>
    <changefreq>weekly</changefreq>
    <priority>1.0</priority>
  </url>
</urlset>
